{{!
    @template tool_vae/state_label

    The state of a declaration as a word, then, after a space, the word that a question waits for an answer when one
    does. Drawn inside a line of text (a paragraph, a summary): it holds no block.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\state_label. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * state - string, the word of the state
    * question - false, or {text}: the word of a question waiting

    Example context (json):
    {
        "state": "Declared",
        "question": {"text": "Question open"}
    }
}}
<span class="badge bg-secondary text-white tool-vae-state">{{state}}</span>{{#question}} {{!
}}<span class="badge bg-info text-dark tool-vae-state">{{text}}</span>{{/question}}
